  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Adaptive Average Pool 2D** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np, math\n\ndef cv_adaptive_avg_pool_2d(image: list, output_size: list) -> list:\n    img = np.array(image, dtype=np.float64)\n    is_2d = (img.ndim == 2)\n    if is_2d: img = img[np.newaxis, :, :]\n    C, H, W = img.shape\n    oh, ow = int(output_size[0]), int(output_size[1])\n    out = np.zeros((C, oh, ow))\n    for c in range(C):\n        for i in range(oh):\n            sh, eh = int(math.floor(i * H / oh)), int(math.ceil((i + 1) * H / oh))\n            for j in range(ow):\n                sw, ew = int(math.floor(j * W / ow)), int(math.ceil((j + 1) * W / ow))\n                out[c, i, j] = np.mean(img[c, sh:eh, sw:ew])\n    return np.round(out[0] if is_2d else out, 6).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
